# Plumbline Scan

When the user asks to check, scan, lint or review a Harbor-format task (a folder with `task.toml`, `tests/`,
`solution/`, `environment/`), or asks whether a grader can be passed without doing the task:

1. Run, from the project root:
   `python3 .cursor/plumbline-scan/run_scan.py <tasks path> --out plumbline-scan-out`
   (static checks PS-7 to PS-12: no Docker, no network). Add `--full` only if the user wants the Docker checks
   PS-1 to PS-6. Exit code 1 means a task was flagged (a result, not an error); exit code 3 means the scanner is
   missing: show the install line it prints.
2. Report the verdict counts and one line per FLAG or WARN (task, check ID, what it found, how to fix). Keep the
   closing caveats.
3. Offer to apply a fix line to the verifier; re-run the scan on that task afterwards.

Never call a task "safe" or "certified": a clean scan does not show the tests are strong enough, and a static flag
is a lead, not proof. Do not upload or send results anywhere.
